## Summary

I implemented the **P4 shared surface 0208 — `DataTable` (Apple)**, a production-grade native SwiftUI parity of `web/src/components/ui/DataTable.tsx`, committed as `d64a379e3` (17 `DataTable.*` files + the gate log).

**Delivered (full parity, no stubs):**
- **16 Swift files**: `Adapter`/`Projection`/`CSV` (Foundation-only pure core), `Services` (telemetry/store/exporter seams), `Strings` (P1/S10 facade), `Model` (P1/S8 `@Observable` holder + once-only `view.opened` P1/S11), `Layout`/`HeaderView`/`RowView`/`ToolbarView`/`StateViews`/`Surface` (token-driven views, P1/S9), `Hooks` (`useSortToggle`/`useTableSelection`/`useTableExpansion` peers), `Previews`, `AdapterTests` + `Tests`; plus `DataTable.strings`.
- Sortable headers, single/multi selection (select-all, indeterminate, shift-range), expansion drawer, column resize/reorder/visibility menu, CSV export (with in-flight spinner), pagination, density, sticky header, mobile allow-list. Every **real** web state reproduced (populated/empty/error/export-loading) and every web `t()` key mirrored 1:1, plus VoiceOver labels.

**Verified within my allowed scope:**
- `swiftlint --strict` (my files): **0 violations**
- `swiftformat --lint` (my files): **0**
- placeholder check: **0** (`PLACEHOLDER_EXIT=0`)
- My files **type-check + SILGen cleanly** (0 errors attributed to any `DataTable.*` file).

**STATUS=BLOCKED (documented in the log, `EXIT=1`).** The gate's `xcodebuild build test` (iOS + macOS) is blocked by a **pre-existing Swift 6.3.2 IRGen crash** (`report_at_maximum_capacity` emitting the `@isolated(any) @Sendable (Bool)->()` thunk) in `AppearanceSettings.Controls.swift` — **proven independent of my surface** by a baseline build with all 16 of my files removed that crashes identically (same SIL symbol, same file; sibling slots hit it too). I fixed two genuine collisions of my own along the way: the filename clash with the pre-existing `Sources/Components/UI/DataTable.swift` (renamed mine to `DataTable.Surface.swift`) and type-name clashes with sibling surfaces (`ColumnLayout`→`DataTableColumnLayout`, inline `DataTableBulkBar`→`DataTableSelectionBulkBar`). The whole-app `swiftlint`/`swiftformat` reds are pre-existing debt in non-`DataTable` files (`WidgetChartSummary.Tests.swift`, `RecentDrivesSection.Previews.swift`) outside my allowed edit scope.

